# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true). run-all.sh is COPYed into the Linux harness image and is
# its ENTRYPOINT: a CRLF checkout makes the shebang read `bash\r`, and the
# container dies with exit 127 / "/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory" before a single test runs.
*.sh text eol=lf
